        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.floridasmart.com/city-guide/homeland"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "Homeland’s roots trace back to the 1850s when settlers first established farms and homesteads.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        18
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.floridasmart.com/city-guide/homeland"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "The South Florida Railroad once stopped in Homeland, linking it to Bartow, Fort Meade, and other towns.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        20
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.floridasmart.com/city-guide/homeland"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Homeland is one of Polk County’s oldest settlements, celebrated for its quiet, rural charm.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        4
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.floridasmart.com/city-guide/homeland"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "Visitors to Homeland Heritage Park can explore historic buildings, learn pioneer life, and watch living‑history demonstrations.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        5
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.floridasmart.com/city-guide/homeland"
    },
    {
